b38 is a text with value "Special characters in text", size 26, weight 800, foreground "#0b1d36", letterspacing "-0.02em", margin "14px 0 0 0"
b39 is a text with value "Text goes between double quotes on one line. A backslash starts an escape, and Otter understands exactly four: \\n is a new line, \\t is a tab, \\\\ is one backslash, and \\\" is a double quote inside the text. There is no \\r. Any other backslash is kept as it is written, so \\q stays \\q.", size 16, foreground "#3a4d6b", lineheight "1.6"
b40 is a text with value "say \"one\\ttwo\"\nsay \"line one\\nline two\"\nsay \"She said \\\"hi\\\"\"\nsay \"a backslash: \\\\\"\nsay \"C:\\\\new\\\\table\"\nsay \"C:/new/table\"", size 14, foreground "#e5edf8", background "#0f1b2e", radius 12, fontfamily "'JetBrains Mono', Consolas, monospace", whitespace "pre", customstyle "padding: 18px 22px; line-height: 1.7; overflow-x: auto; border-top-left-radius: 0; border-top-right-radius: 0;", runnable true
